  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EFI-St&#xf6;d till politisk &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ng i Syrien genom k&#xf6;nsk&#xe4;nslig social &#xe5;teruppbyggnad</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EFI-Support political transition in Syria with gender-sensitive social reconstru - Old Strategy- Support political transition in Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Euromed Feminist Initiative (EFI) har presenterat ett projektf&#xf6;rslag om 75 000 000 SEK f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra projektet &quot;Supporting political transition in Syria through gender-sensitive social reconstruction&quot;. Sida har tidigare st&#xf6;tt EFIs genomf&#xf6;rande av ett liknande projekt, med positiva erfarenheter. 

Projektet syftar till att uppn&#xe5; f&#xf6;ljande m&#xe5;l:

- Minskat v&#xe5;ld mot kvinnor och flickor (VAWG) och konfliktrelaterat sexuellt v&#xe5;ld (CRSV) och fr&#xe4;mjande av kvinnors deltagande i beslutsfattande, fred och nationella f&#xf6;rsoningsprocesser fr&#xe4;mjas.

- St&#xe4;rkt institutionell kapacitet f&#xf6;r civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer (CSO) och tillhandah&#xe5;llande av tematisk kunskap.

- Fr&#xe4;mjande av inkluderande demokratiska f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar genom k&#xf6;nsrelaterade juridiska och politiska f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar och WR-framsteg.

Insatsens totala budget omfattar 75 miljoner kronor som helt finansieras av Sida, varav cirka 40% kommer att vidarebefordras till partner organisationer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Euromed Feminist Initiative (EFI) has submitted a project proposal to request for 75 000 000 SEK to implement &quot;Supporting political transition in Syria through gender-sensitive social reconstruction&quot;. Sida has previously supported the implementation a similar project, with positive experiences.

This intervention aims at achieving the following objectives: 

- Violence Against Women and Girls (VAWG) and Conflict Related Sexual Violence (CRSV) are better addressed and women&#x2019;s participation in decision making, peace and national reconciliation processes is promoted;

-Institutional capacities of Civil Society Organizations (CSOs) are strengthened and provision of thematic knowledge is structured;

-Inclusive democratic change is promoted through fostering gender sensitive legal and policy changes and WR advancement.

The intervention&#x2019;s total budget is 75 million SEK fully funded by Sida of which around 40% will be forwarded to partner organizations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is to contribute to inclusive gender-sensitive peace-building and social reconstruction process in Syria. The specific objectives of the intervention that are intended to be achieved at the end of the intervention are the following:
- Violence Against Women and Girls (VAWG) and Conflict Related Sexual Violence (CRSV) are better addressed and women&#x2019;s participation in decision making, peace and national reconciliation processes is promoted;
-Institutional capacities of Civil Society Organizations (CSOs) are strengthened and provision of thematic knowledge is structured;
-Inclusive democratic change is promoted through fostering gender sensitive legal and policy changes and WR advancement.</narrative>
  </description>
